# DeanOS & GitHub Organization Plan

The goal is to provide a comprehensive status report for the DeanOS server, establish a "one-click" SSH command for Coolify health/activation, and reorganize the messy GitHub/local project structure.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - I will be adding a `Coolify: Status & Fix` command to your `zima.ps1` script. This will automatically fix the "Permission Denied" errors I detected in Coolify's logs.
> - For the GitHub/Local project mess, I propose moving "one-off" experiments to an `Archive` folder to simplify your view in `c:\projects`.
> - Do you want me to also help you Archive/Consolidate your GitHub repositories online?

## Proposed Changes

### DeanOS & Coolify Control

#### [MODIFY] [zima.ps1](file:///d:/OS/Zimaos/zima.ps1)
- Add a new menu option: `10. 🧊 Coolify Sağlık Kotrolü & Tamir`
- This command will:
  - Check if Coolify and its dependencies (Redis, Postgres, Soketi) are running.
  - Run a `chmod` fix for the storage/logs folder on the server to resolve the "Permission Denied" errors.
  - Restart the Coolify container if it's unhealthy.

### GitHub & Project Organization

#### [NEW] [Organization Strategy]
- Move "Boilerplate" and "MVP" projects in `c:\projects` to structured subfolders:
  - `c:\projects\Development` (Active items like `it-inventory`, `evaiteclabs`)
  - `c:\projects\Archive` (One-off experiments like `Quiz`, `food-delivery-mock`)
  - `c:\projects\Boilerplates` (Templates like `saas-starter-kit`, `myllm`)
- This will make your daily workflow much cleaner.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
